1
00:02:44,444 --> 00:02:50,444
Forbidden Zone is a music, comedy, fantasy film directed by Richard Elfman.

2
00:05:28,888 --> 00:05:34,888
A mysterious door in the basement of the Hercules house leads to the
Sixth Dimension by way of a gigantic set of intestine.

3
00:08:13,333 --> 00:08:19,333
When Frenchy slips through the door, King Fausto falls in love with her.

4
00:10:57,777 --> 00:11:03,777
The jealous Queen Doris takes Frenchy prisoner, and it is up to the
Hercules family and friend Squeezit Henderson to rescue her.

5
00:13:42,222 --> 00:13:48,222
King Fausto of the Sixth Dimension, played by Hervé Villechaize.

6
00:16:26,666 --> 00:16:32,666
Queen Doris of the Sixth Dimension, played by Susan Tyrrell.

7
00:19:11,111 --> 00:19:17,111
Squeezit & René Henderson, played by Matthew Bright.

8
00:21:55,555 --> 00:22:01,555
Pa Hercules, played by Gene Cunningham.

9
00:24:40,000 --> 00:24:46,000
Susan B. "Frenchie" Hercules, played by Marie-Pascale Elfman.

10
00:27:24,444 --> 00:27:30,444
Ma Hercules, played by Virginia Rose.

11
00:30:08,888 --> 00:30:14,888
Forbidden Zone is an American absurdist musical fantasy comedy film produced and directed by
independent filmmaker Richard Elfman, and co-written by Elfman and Matthew Bright.

12
00:32:53,333 --> 00:32:59,333
Shot in 1977 and 1978, the film premiered in 1980 and was distributed in 1982.

13
00:35:37,777 --> 00:35:43,777
Originally shot on black-and-white film, Forbidden Zone is based upon the stage performances of the Los Angeles theater troupe The Mystic Knights of the Oingo Boingo, of which
Elfman, Bright and many of the cast and crew were a part, and revolves around an alternate universe accessed through a door in the house of the Hercules family.

14
00:38:22,222 --> 00:38:28,222
The composing debut of Danny Elfman, it stars Hervé Villechaize, Susan Tyrrell and members of the
Mystic Knights, with appearances by Warhol superstar Viva, Joe Spinell and The Kipper Kids.

15
00:41:06,666 --> 00:41:12,666
Villechaize kicked his cheque back into production
and even painted sets on weekends.

16
00:43:51,111 --> 00:43:57,111
The only paid actor was Phil Gordon, who played Flash; all the
other SAG actors put their money back into the show.

17
00:46:35,555 --> 00:46:41,555
The film was made as an attempt to capture the essence of The Mystic Knights of the Oingo Boingo's live performances in a cinematic sense, and also as a means for both
director Elfman to retire from music to work on film projects, and to serve as a transition between the group's former cabaret style and a new wave-based style.

18
00:49:20,000 --> 00:49:26,000
Amid negative reactions to content in the film that had been perceived as being offensive, Forbidden Zone was screened as a
midnight movie, where it was met with positive notices, and developed a large and eventually worldwide cult following.

19
00:52:04,444 --> 00:52:10,444
In 2004, the film was digitally restored and released on
DVD, and in 2008, the film was colorized.

20
00:54:48,888 --> 00:54:54,888
Said Elfman, "Doing anything original is taking a chance.

21
00:57:33,333 --> 00:57:39,333
Financially it bankrupted me and we lost our house.

22
01:00:17,777 --> 01:00:23,777
But I'm still glad I did it (although I'd change a few things if I had a time machine, of course)."
A prospective sequel, entitled Forbidden Zone 2: The
Forbidden Galaxy, has long been in development by Elfman, who launched a successful crowdfunding campaign in 2014 to raise an initial sum.

23
01:03:02,222 --> 01:03:08,222
As of 2019, the sequel is still in the stages of development
but regularly updated and discussed by Elfman.

24
01:05:46,666 --> 01:05:52,666
Elfman has also licensed Forbidden Zone as an intellectual property for
manufacturers to produce collectibles based on the film's characters.

25
01:08:31,111 --> 01:08:37,111
The film explores themes of musical, satan, sexual
violence, incest, rock musical.

26
01:11:15,555 --> 01:11:21,555
The tone is lighthearted and mind_bending.
